adjudication.rationale:
In `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the webhook authentication compares the provided secret to `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` using a direct `!==` string comparison:

```ts
if (req.headers[... ] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403).json({ message: "Invalid webhook secret" });
}
```

This is not a constant-time comparison (unlike `crypto.timingSafeEqual`) and therefore can, in principle, leak information via timing differences. The issue described in the finding is directly present in the diff.
